  "brief_md": "## O02 — Decision Intelligence Tool (reframe decision, research market/competitors, present trade-offs)\n\n### Payer\nHypothesized payer: individual operators, strategists, consultants, or product leaders, likely expensing or self-funding a per-decision or monthly tool. Price anchor: Foray sells comparable AI-generated strategic blueprints from **$60/blueprint** or **$299/mo** professional plan ([getforay.ai](https://www.getforay.ai/)); MarketGeist anchors lower at **$49/mo** Starter ([marketgeist.com/pricing](https://marketgeist.com/pricing)).\n\n### Competitors\n- **Foray** — $60/blueprint, $299/mo pro (getforay.ai)\n- **MarketGeist** — $49/mo Starter, Pro/Enterprise tiers unlisted (marketgeist.com/pricing)\n- **Insightloop** — $99/mo founding tier, pre-launch (getinsightloop.com)\n- **PREONZ** — pricing NOT FOUND (preonz.com/solutions)\n- **Gixo.ai** — per-workspace pricing, e.g. $10/mo Prism workspace (gixo.ai/pricing)\n\nAll five position themselves almost identically to O02: AI agents that research a market/competitors and hand back a structured, 'evidence-backed' or 'decision-ready' document. This is a dense, active niche, not a greenfield one.\n\n### Acquisition\n- Google Ads, Business Services vertical: ~**$103.54 average cost-per-lead** (WordStream 2025 benchmarks).\n- LinkedIn Ads, B2B SaaS targeting: **$8–$12 CPC** (Aimers.io benchmark).\nBoth are expensive relative to a $60 one-off product; organic/community channels (Indie Hackers, LinkedIn posts where this pain is voiced natively) look cheaper but slower and unquantified.\n\n### Demand evidence\nReal operators describe the underlying pain of being stuck between 'reasonable' options and wanting outside structure to force a decision:\n- \"Different directions, different options and most of them are…reasonable. That's where it gets tricky.\" — Indie Hackers post, 2026 ([link](https://www.indiehackers.com/post/when-everything-feels-equally-valid-how-do-you-actually-decide-7fec917ca0))\n- \"Once you've got 2 real options, the spreadsheet can't choose between them. Only you can.\" — LinkedIn post, 2026 ([link](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/omerkhan_a-founder-asked-for-my-help-with-a-decision-activity-7498371372146999296-dzyz))\n\n### Case for\nThe agentic research-and-document pipeline this idea requires is already proven buildable by small teams (Foray's sequenced specialist agents, Gixo's multi-stage pipeline), so a solo founder with AI agents likely *can* build a working version in six weeks. Real operators articulate this exact pain unprompted, and several funded-looking competitors already charge $49–$299/mo for adjacent versions, which both validates willingness to pay and gives a concrete price anchor.\n\n### Case against\nThe niche is already saturated with near-identical pitches (Foray's Adversarial Review/Kill Conditions, MarketGeist's Decision Brief, PREONZ's option comparisons) built by teams with more data infrastructure (MarketGeist: 250+ live sources, continuous monitoring) than a six-week solo build can match. The category's own vendors admit a core trust problem — Gixo states uploaded-source figures are the only 'sourced' ones and that a human must verify every number and recommendation before acting — undermining the premise that the tool alone delivers a decision-ready output. Paid acquisition costs (~$104 CPL) sit awkwardly against a ~$60 one-off price point, squeezing unit economics without a strong organic channel.\n\n### Open questions\nSee `open_questions` field — chiefly: what is the differentiated wedge versus Foray/MarketGeist, what monetization model fits episodic 'big decision' usage, and would users simply default to a general-purpose LLM chat instead of a dedicated tool."
